    "lang": "vi_explain",
    "stem": "Consider the decision table for the portion of an online airline reservation system that allows frequent flyers to redeem points for reward travel (see the figure). Suppose there are two equivalence partitions for the condition where “Account/password okay” is not true (invalid account; valid account but invalid password), and only one partition where it is true. If you want to design tests to cover the equivalence partitions for “Account/password okay” and also this portion of the decision table, what is the minimum number of tests required?",
