    "k_level": "",
    "lang": "vi_explain",
    "stem": "You must compile a test execution schedule. The system has these logical dependencies: an ADMIN user must create/amend/delete a STANDARD user, and a standard user is necessary to perform all other actions. The test plan requires: re-tests (previously failed tests) must be performed first, followed by the highest-priority tests; and tests should be scheduled so that they create the test data needed by subsequent tests. The test cases are shown in the figure: (a) log in as standard user and create a customer account — priority 2, previously failed; (b) order one item — priority 3, passed; (c) create an invoice for an order — priority 1, previously failed; (d) order two items or more — priority 3, previously failed; (e) log in as admin user and create a standard user — priority 2, passed. Which schedule meets the test plan requirements and the logical dependencies?",
